/-!
# The relative differentials of a blowup are carried by the exceptional divisor

Let `S` be a scheme, let `p : Z ⟶ S` be a closed immersion with ideal sheaf `ℐ = ker(p)` and let
`b : X ⟶ S` be the blowup of `S` in `ℐ`, with exceptional divisor `i : E ⟶ X`. The exceptional
ideal `ℐ·𝒪_X` annihilates `Ω_{X/S}`: on the affine chart `Γ(S, V)[ℐ(V)/a]` the relation
`a · (y/a) = y` forces `a · d(y/a) = 0`, hence `a · Ω` and therefore `ℐ(V) · Ω` vanish. Since `E`
is the fibre product `X ×_S Z`, the sheaf of relative differentials of `E` over `Z` is the
pullback `i^* Ω_{X/S}`, and the annihilation identifies `Ω_{X/S}` with its own direct image from
`E`:

`Ω_{X/S} = i_* Ω_{E/Z}`.

For `S = Spec(A)` with `(A, 𝔪, κ)` a regular local ring of dimension two and `Z` the closed point
this is the differentials computation of the quadratic transformation of a regular surface.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalToCentre`: the structure morphism `E ⟶ Z` of the exceptional divisor
  over the centre of the blowup, the lift of `E ⟶ X ⟶ S` through the closed immersion `p`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.relativeDifferentialsToPushforward`: the canonical map
  `Ω_{X/S} ⟶ i_* Ω_{E/Z}`, the adjoint transpose of the functorial map `i^*Ω_{X/S} ⟶ Ω_{E/Z}` of
  Stacks tag 01UV for the square `(i, exceptionalToCentre, b, p)`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.residuePoint`: the closed point of the spectrum of a local ring.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Blowup.smul_kaehlerDifferential_affineBlowup_eq_zero` and
  `Stacks.Blowup.smul_kaehlerDifferential_affineBlowup_eq_zero_of_mem`: the element `a`, and
  then every element of `I`, annihilates `Ω_{R[I/a]/R}`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal_smul_relativeDifferentials_eq_zero`: the exceptional ideal
  annihilates the sections of `Ω_{X/S}` over every open, and
  `Stacks.Blowup.isIso_unit_relativeDifferentials`: the unit `Ω_{X/S} ⟶ i_* i^* Ω_{X/S}` is
  therefore an isomorphism.
* `Stacks.Blowup.isPullback_exceptionalToCentre`: the exceptional divisor is the fibre product
  of the blowup with the centre.
* `Stacks.Blowup.isIso_relativeDifferentialsToPushforward`: the canonical map
  `Ω_{X/S} ⟶ i_* Ω_{E/Z}` is an isomorphism.
* `Stacks.Blowup.ker_residuePoint`: the ideal sheaf of the closed point of `Spec(A)` is the
  maximal ideal of `A`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.isIso_relativeDifferentialsToPushforward_residuePoint`: the same isomorphism for
  the blowup of a regular local ring of dimension two in its maximal ideal, which is Stacks
  tag 0B4L.

## Implementation notes

The annihilation is proved on the charts of Stacks tag 0804
(`Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart`), which cover the blowup, and then spread over an arbitrary
open in three steps: on an affine open `W` contained in the image of a chart
`Spec Γ(S, V)[ℐ(V)/a]` the sections of `Ω_{X/S}` are the Kähler differentials of
`Γ(S, V) ⟶ Γ(X, W)` by Stacks tag 01UT, and `Γ(X, W)` is étale, hence formally unramified, over
the chart ring, so `KaehlerDifferential.mapBaseChange` is surjective and the annihilation
transfers; the exceptional ideal on `W` is generated by the images of `ℐ(V)` by
`Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE`; and equality of sections of a sheaf is local, so an
arbitrary open is covered by such `W`.

Two spellings of the sections of a sheaf of modules are in play, as recorded in
`Stacks.ClosedImmersion.pushforward_essImage_iff`: the `Γ`-spelling, at which the `Module`
instance is found, and the `ModuleCat`-object spelling, in which the comparison isomorphism of
Stacks tag 01UT lives. They are definitionally equal, and
`Stacks.Blowup.smul_sections_relativeDifferentials_eq_zero_of_chart` passes between them by
`show` and by one local `Module` instance; mixing them inside a single expression does not
elaborate.

The identification of the exceptional divisor with `X ×_S Z` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.isPullback_of_isClosedImmersion`, whose hypothesis is exactly
`ker(p).comap b = ker(i)`, and the structure morphism over the centre is
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsClosedImmersion.lift`; neither needs any identification of the exceptional
divisor with a projective line, so nothing of Stacks tag 0AGQ beyond the blowup itself is used.
The final isomorphism is `Adjunction.homEquiv_unit`: the adjoint transpose of the functorial map
is the unit followed by the direct image of that map, the unit is invertible by Stacks tag 08KS
and the annihilation, and the functorial map is invertible by Stacks tag 01V0.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B4L](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B4L)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01V0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01V0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01UT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01UT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08KS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08KS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0804](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0804)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.Blowup

/-! ### The affine blowup algebra -/

/-- In a subalgebra generated by elements `z` for which `a · z` is a scalar, the scalar `a`
annihilates the universal differential of every element. -/
private theorem smul_d_adjoin_eq_zero {R T : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing T] [Algebra R T]
    (a : R) (s : Set T) (hs : ∀ z ∈ s, ∃ y : R, algebraMap R T a * z = algebraMap R T y)
    (z : Algebra.adjoin R s) :
    algebraMap R (Algebra.adjoin R s) a •
      KaehlerDifferential.D R (Algebra.adjoin R s) z = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := z
  induction hz using Algebra.adjoin_induction with
  | mem x hx =>
      obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := hs x hx
      have key : algebraMap R (Algebra.adjoin R s) a *
            (⟨x, Algebra.subset_adjoin hx⟩ : Algebra.adjoin R s) =
          algebraMap R (Algebra.adjoin R s) y := Subtype.ext hy
      have hD := congrArg (KaehlerDifferential.D R (Algebra.adjoin R s)) key
      simpa only [(KaehlerDifferential.D R (Algebra.adjoin R s)).leibniz,
        Derivation.map_algebraMap, smul_zero, add_zero] using hD
  | algebraMap r =>
      rw [show (⟨algebraMap R T r, _⟩ : Algebra.adjoin R s) = algebraMap R _ r from rfl,
        Derivation.map_algebraMap, smul_zero]
  | add x y hx hy ihx ihy =>
      rw [show (⟨x + y, add_mem hx hy⟩ : Algebra.adjoin R s) = ⟨x, hx⟩ + ⟨y, hy⟩ from rfl,
        map_add, smul_add, ihx, ihy, add_zero]
  | mul x y hx hy ihx ihy =>
      rw [show (⟨x * y, mul_mem hx hy⟩ : Algebra.adjoin R s) = ⟨x, hx⟩ * ⟨y, hy⟩ from rfl,
        (KaehlerDifferential.D R (Algebra.adjoin R s)).leibniz, smul_add, smul_comm, ihy,
        smul_comm, ihx, smul_zero, smul_zero, add_zero]

/-- The same annihilation on all of the Kähler differentials, the universal differentials
spanning them. -/
private theorem smul_kaehler_adjoin_eq_zero {R T : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing T] [Algebra R T]
    (a : R) (s : Set T) (hs : ∀ z ∈ s, ∃ y : R, algebraMap R T a * z = algebraMap R T y)
    (ω : KaehlerDifferential R (Algebra.adjoin R s)) :
    algebraMap R (Algebra.adjoin R s) a • ω = 0 := by
  have hω : ω ∈ Submodule.span (Algebra.adjoin R s)
      (Set.range (KaehlerDifferential.D R (Algebra.adjoin R s))) := by
    rw [KaehlerDifferential.span_range_derivation]
    exact Submodule.mem_top
  induction hω using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem w hw => obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := hw; exact smul_d_adjoin_eq_zero a s hs z
  | zero => exact smul_zero _
  | add x y _ _ hx hy => rw [smul_add, hx, hy, add_zero]
  | smul c x _ hx => rw [smul_comm, hx, smul_zero]

/-- In `R[1/a]`, the fraction `y/a` satisfies `a · (y/a) = y`. -/
private theorem algebraMap_mul_mk_eq {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (a y : R) :
    algebraMap R (Localization.Away a) a * Localization.mk y ⟨a, Submonoid.mem_powers a⟩ =
      algebraMap R (Localization.Away a) y := by
  rw [← Localization.mk_one_eq_algebraMap, ← Localization.mk_one_eq_algebraMap,
    Localization.mk_mul, Localization.mk_eq_mk_iff, Localization.r_iff_exists]
  exact ⟨1, by simp [mul_comm]⟩

/-- **The denominator of an affine blowup algebra annihilates its relative differentials.** In
`R[I/a]` the fraction `y/a` satisfies `a · (y/a) = y`, so `a · d(y/a) = 0`, and the fractions
`y/a` with `y ∈ I` generate `R[I/a]` over `R`. -/
theorem smul_kaehlerDifferential_affineBlowup_eq_zero {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R)
    (a : R) (ω : KaehlerDifferential R (affineBlowup I a)) :
    algebraMap R (affineBlowup I a) a • ω = 0 :=
  smul_kaehler_adjoin_eq_zero a (affineBlowupGenSet I a)
    (fun z hz => by
      obtain ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩ := hz
      exact ⟨y, algebraMap_mul_mk_eq a y⟩) ω

/-- **The centre of a blowup annihilates the relative differentials of an affine chart.** Every
`y ∈ I` is `a · (y/a)` in `R[I/a]`, so it annihilates what `a` annihilates. -/
theorem smul_kaehlerDifferential_affineBlowup_eq_zero_of_mem {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    (I : Ideal R) (a : R) {y : R} (hy : y ∈ I)
    (ω : KaehlerDifferential R (affineBlowup I a)) :
    algebraMap R (affineBlowup I a) y • ω = 0 := by
  have hq : (Localization.mk y ⟨a, Submonoid.mem_powers a⟩ : Localization.Away a) ∈
      affineBlowup I a := Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
  have hfrac : algebraMap R (affineBlowup I a) y =
      algebraMap R (affineBlowup I a) a * ⟨_, hq⟩ := by
    exact Subtype.ext (algebraMap_mul_mk_eq a y).symm
  have hz := smul_kaehlerDifferential_affineBlowup_eq_zero I a
    ((⟨_, hq⟩ : affineBlowup I a) • ω)
  rw [hfrac]
  exact (mul_smul (algebraMap R (affineBlowup I a) a) ⟨_, hq⟩ ω).trans hz

/-! ### Annihilation of the sections of the sheaf of differentials -/

/-- Annihilation of Kähler differentials passes to a formally unramified extension, because
`KaehlerDifferential.mapBaseChange` is then surjective. -/
private theorem smul_kaehler_eq_zero_of_formallyUnramified {R B C : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [CommRing B] [CommRing C] [Algebra R B] [Algebra B C] [Algebra R C] [IsScalarTower R B C]
    [Algebra.FormallyUnramified B C] {y : R}
    (hy : ∀ ω : KaehlerDifferential R B, algebraMap R B y • ω = 0)
    (ω : KaehlerDifferential R C) : algebraMap R C y • ω = 0 := by
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (KaehlerDifferential.mapBaseChange R B C) := by
    rw [← LinearMap.range_eq_top, KaehlerDifferential.range_mapBaseChange]
    exact LinearMap.ker_eq_top.mpr (Subsingleton.elim _ _)
  obtain ⟨t, rfl⟩ := hsurj ω
  induction t using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | add x z hx hz => simp only [map_add, smul_add, hx, hz, add_zero]
  | tmul c b =>
      rw [KaehlerDifferential.mapBaseChange_tmul, smul_comm]
      have h := congrArg (KaehlerDifferential.map R R B C) (hy b)
      rw [map_smul, map_zero] at h
      have h' : algebraMap R C y • KaehlerDifferential.map R R B C b = 0 := by
        simpa only [← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R B C,
          IsScalarTower.algebraMap_smul] using h
      rw [h', smul_zero]

/-- A scalar annihilating the Kähler differentials of an affine chart over `V` annihilates the
sections of `Ω_{X/S}` on every affine open contained in the image of that chart. -/
private theorem smul_sections_relativeDifferentials_eq_zero_of_chart {X S : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X ⟶ S) {V : S.Opens} (hV : IsAffineOpen V) (B : Type u) [CommRing B]
    [Algebra Γ(S, V) B] (j : Spec (.of B) ⟶ X) [IsOpenImmersion j]
    (hj : j ≫ f = Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(S, V) B)) ≫ hV.fromSpec)
    {W : X.Opens} (hW : IsAffineOpen W) (hWj : (W : Set X) ⊆ Set.range j)
    (hWV : W ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V) {y : Γ(S, V)}
    (hy : ∀ ω : KaehlerDifferential Γ(S, V) B, algebraMap Γ(S, V) B y • ω = 0)
    (m : Γ(Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials f, W)) :
    (f.appLE V W hWV).hom y • m = 0 := by
  let C := Γ(X, W)
  let k : Spec (.of C) ⟶ Spec (.of B) :=
    IsOpenImmersion.lift j hW.fromSpec (hW.range_fromSpec.le.trans hWj)
  have hk : k ≫ j = hW.fromSpec := IsOpenImmersion.lift_fac _ _ _
  have : IsOpenImmersion (k ≫ j) := by rw [hk]; infer_instance
  have : IsOpenImmersion k := IsOpenImmersion.of_comp k j
  let b : B →+* C := (Spec.preimage k).hom
  have hb : Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom b) = k := Spec.map_preimage k
  let : Algebra B C := b.toAlgebra
  let : Algebra Γ(S, V) C := (f.appLE V W hWV).hom.toAlgebra
  have hspec : Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (b.comp (algebraMap Γ(S, V) B))) =
      Spec.map (f.appLE V W hWV) := by
    refine (cancel_mono hV.fromSpec).mp ?_
    rw [IsAffineOpen.SpecMap_appLE_fromSpec f hV hW hWV,
      show CommRingCat.ofHom (b.comp (algebraMap Γ(S, V) B)) =
        CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(S, V) B) ≫ CommRingCat.ofHom b from rfl,
      Spec.map_comp, hb, Category.assoc, ← hj, ← Category.assoc, hk]
  have htower : b.comp (algebraMap Γ(S, V) B) = (f.appLE V W hWV).hom :=
    CommRingCat.hom_ext_iff.mp (Spec.map_injective hspec)
  let : IsScalarTower Γ(S, V) B C := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' htower.symm
  have hfu : b.FormallyUnramified := by
    apply (HasRingHomProperty.Spec_iff (P := @FormallyUnramified)).mp
    rw [Spec.map_preimage]
    infer_instance
  let : Algebra.FormallyUnramified B C := hfu
  obtain ⟨e, -, -⟩ :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineDifferentialsIso.existsUnique_affineDifferentialsIso f hW hWV hV
  change (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials f).val.obj (op W) ≅
    ModuleCat.of C (KaehlerDifferential Γ(S, V) C) at e
  let : Module ↑(X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W)) (KaehlerDifferential Γ(S, V) C) :=
    inferInstanceAs (Module C (KaehlerDifferential Γ(S, V) C))
  have hsm : (ModuleCat.Hom.hom e.hom) ((f.appLE V W hWV).hom y • m) =
      (f.appLE V W hWV).hom y • (ModuleCat.Hom.hom e.hom) m :=
    (ModuleCat.Hom.hom e.hom).map_smul
      (show ↑(X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W)) from (f.appLE V W hWV).hom y) m
  have hinj : Function.Injective (ModuleCat.Hom.hom e.hom) := e.toLinearEquiv.injective
  exact hinj (hsm.trans
    ((smul_kaehler_eq_zero_of_formallyUnramified hy (ModuleCat.Hom.hom e.hom m)).trans
      ((ModuleCat.Hom.hom e.hom).map_zero).symm))

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} (ℐ : S.IdealSheafData)

/-- If the restriction of `a` to `W ≤ U` kills every section over `W`, the restriction of
`a • m` to `W` is `0`. -/
private theorem restrict_smul_relativeDifferentials_eq_zero {U W : (blowUp ℐ).Opens} (h : W ≤ U)
    (a : Γ(blowUp ℐ, U)) (m : Γ(Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials (blowUpToBase ℐ), U))
    (hz : ∀ n : Γ(Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials (blowUpToBase ℐ), W),
      (blowUp ℐ).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op a • n = 0) :
    (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials (blowUpToBase ℐ)).val.map (homOfLE h).op (a • m) = 0 :=
  ((Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials (blowUpToBase ℐ)).val.map_smul (homOfLE h).op a m).trans
    (hz _)

/-- **The exceptional ideal annihilates the sections of `Ω_{X/S}` on an affine open.** Every
point of the affine open lies in one of the charts of Stacks tag 0804, so a smaller affine open
is covered by `Stacks.Blowup.smul_sections_relativeDifferentials_eq_zero_of_chart`, and equality
of sections of a sheaf is local. -/
private theorem smul_sections_relativeDifferentials_eq_zero_of_affineOpens
    (W : (blowUp ℐ).affineOpens) (a : Γ(blowUp ℐ, W.1))
    (ha : a ∈ (exceptionalIdeal ℐ).ideal W)
    (m : Γ(Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials (blowUpToBase ℐ), W.1)) : a • m = 0 := by
  classical
  apply (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials (blowUpToBase ℐ)).isSheaf.section_ext (U := op W.1)
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨V, hV, rfl⟩, hxV, -⟩ := S.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open
    (Set.mem_univ ((blowUpToBase ℐ).base x)) isOpen_univ
  have hxpre : x ∈ blowUpToBase ℐ ⁻¹ᵁ ((⟨V, hV⟩ : S.affineOpens) : S.Opens) := hxV
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := Opens.mem_iSup.mp
    ((iSup_opensRange_blowUpAffineChart ℐ ⟨V, hV⟩).symm ▸ hxpre)
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨Wc, hWc, rfl⟩, hxWc, hWsub⟩ :=
    (blowUp ℐ).isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open
      (show x ∈ (W.1 ⊓ (blowUpAffineChart ℐ ⟨V, hV⟩ r.2).opensRange) from ⟨hx, hr⟩)
      (W.1 ⊓ (blowUpAffineChart ℐ ⟨V, hV⟩ r.2).opensRange).2
  have hWcW : Wc ≤ W.1 := fun _ h => (hWsub h).1
  have hWcj : (Wc : Set (blowUp ℐ)) ⊆ Set.range (blowUpAffineChart ℐ ⟨V, hV⟩ r.2) :=
    fun _ h => (hWsub h).2
  have hWcV : Wc ≤ blowUpToBase ℐ ⁻¹ᵁ V := fun z hz =>
    (iSup_opensRange_blowUpAffineChart ℐ ⟨V, hV⟩).le (Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨r, hWcj hz⟩)
  refine ⟨Wc, hWcW, hxWc, ?_⟩
  have hres : (blowUp ℐ).presheaf.map (homOfLE hWcW).op a ∈
      (exceptionalIdeal ℐ).ideal ⟨Wc, hWc⟩ :=
    (exceptionalIdeal ℐ).ideal_le_comap_ideal (U := ⟨Wc, hWc⟩) (V := W) hWcW ha
  have hkill : (exceptionalIdeal ℐ).ideal ⟨Wc, hWc⟩ ≤
      Module.annihilator Γ(blowUp ℐ, Wc)
        Γ(Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials (blowUpToBase ℐ), Wc) := by
    rw [exceptionalIdeal, Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE ℐ (blowUpToBase ℐ) ⟨V, hV⟩
        ⟨Wc, hWc⟩ hWcV, Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
    intro y hy
    rw [Ideal.mem_comap, Module.mem_annihilator]
    exact fun n => smul_sections_relativeDifferentials_eq_zero_of_chart (blowUpToBase ℐ) hV
      (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal ⟨V, hV⟩) r.1) (blowUpAffineChart ℐ ⟨V, hV⟩ r.2)
      (blowUpAffineChart_blowUpToBase ℐ ⟨V, hV⟩ r.2) hWc hWcj hWcV
      (fun ω => smul_kaehlerDifferential_affineBlowup_eq_zero_of_mem (ℐ.ideal ⟨V, hV⟩) r.1 hy ω) n
  rw [map_zero]
  exact restrict_smul_relativeDifferentials_eq_zero ℐ hWcW a m
    (Module.mem_annihilator.mp (hkill hres))

/-- **The exceptional ideal of a blowup annihilates its relative differentials.** On an affine
chart the blowup is `Γ(S, V)[ℐ(V)/a]`, in which `a` kills every differential, and the
exceptional ideal there is generated by the image of `ℐ(V)`. -/
theorem exceptionalIdeal_smul_relativeDifferentials_eq_zero (U : (blowUp ℐ).Opens)
    (a : Γ(blowUp ℐ, U))
    (ha : ((exceptionalIdeal ℐ).subschemeι.app U).hom a = 0)
    (m : Γ(Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials (blowUpToBase ℐ), U)) : a • m = 0 := by
  classical
  apply (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials (blowUpToBase ℐ)).isSheaf.section_ext (U := op U)
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨W, hW, rfl⟩, hxW, hWU⟩ :=
    (blowUp ℐ).isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open hx U.2
  refine ⟨W, hWU, hxW, ?_⟩
  have hmem : (blowUp ℐ).presheaf.map (homOfLE (show W ≤ U from hWU)).op a ∈
      (exceptionalIdeal ℐ).ideal ⟨W, hW⟩ := by
    rw [← Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_subschemeι (exceptionalIdeal ℐ),
      Scheme.Hom.ker_apply (exceptionalIdeal ℐ).subschemeι ⟨W, hW⟩]
    refine RingHom.mem_ker.mpr ?_
    have hnat := (exceptionalIdeal ℐ).subschemeι.naturality
      (homOfLE (show W ≤ U from hWU)).op
    have he := congrArg (fun φ : Γ(blowUp ℐ, U) ⟶
      Γ((exceptionalIdeal ℐ).subscheme, (exceptionalIdeal ℐ).subschemeι ⁻¹ᵁ W) => φ.hom a) hnat
    simpa only [CommRingCat.comp_apply, ha, map_zero] using he
  rw [map_zero]
  exact restrict_smul_relativeDifferentials_eq_zero ℐ hWU a m
    (smul_sections_relativeDifferentials_eq_zero_of_affineOpens ℐ ⟨W, hW⟩ _ hmem)

/-- **The relative differentials of a blowup come from the exceptional divisor.** The unit
`Ω_{X/S} ⟶ i_* i^* Ω_{X/S}` of the pullback–direct image adjunction along the exceptional divisor
is an isomorphism, by Stacks tag 08KS and the annihilation. -/
theorem isIso_unit_relativeDifferentials :
    IsIso ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction
      (exceptionalIdeal ℐ).subschemeι).unit.app
        (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials (blowUpToBase ℐ))) :=
  Stacks.ClosedImmersion.isIso_unit_app_of_smul_eq_zero _ _
    (exceptionalIdeal_smul_relativeDifferentials_eq_zero ℐ)

/-! ### The exceptional divisor as the fibre product with the centre -/

variable {Z : Scheme.{u}} (p : Z ⟶ S) [IsClosedImmersion p]

omit [IsClosedImmersion p] in
/-- The kernel of the closed immersion cutting out the centre is below the kernel of the
structure morphism of the exceptional divisor over the base.

